{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000de85","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0894a-0cb5-7fb2-a6c2-26593f708551"},"sequence":3485,"recorded_at":1780531400006965,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"6ef794f5-c8fc-4d82-b028-da1c8560a2dc","payload_type":"run.terminal.completed","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"run_terminal","command_id":"6ef794f5-c8fc-4d82-b028-da1c8560a2dc","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"6ef794f5-c8fc-4d82-b028-da1c8560a2dc"},"terminal":"completed","text":"Ready for review — handed off to `to-review` (checklist 19/19).\n\n**What was done (CR8 P1):** the checkpoint event-head gate checked digests/tuples but never profile authority, so a first launch citing a dangling source was admitted by all four entries. Added shared admission `checkCheckpointProfileAuthority` in [lease.go](/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/STORY-260830-3tq4ns/worktree/internal/sessquery/lease.go) (called after the heads gate for winner + every necessary ancestor via `winningLeaseFor`, so `BuildPlan`, fresh/old-plan `Revalidate`, `AuthoritativeStatus`, `AuthoritativeList` all enforce it). It walks the transitive predecessor closure from the winning-source chain, reads the creation profile via `GetRecord`, and pins first-launch → (creation, null) and later launch/resume → newest in-closure `profile.changed` with its target; violations refuse `integrity_failure` per SPEC 5.4.\n\n**Evidence (all observed, real exits):**\n- RED baseline recorded pre-fix (4 controls pass, 4 negatives admitted); ported probe now 8/8 green.\n- New `rev8_regression_test.go`: real-change positives (launch/resume/two-generation, direct/task_board, winner/ancestor, fresh revalidation), 8 refusal classes with integrity pinned (incl. losing-branch via a preserved divergent blob), historical-closure admission, old-plan profile-only substitution.\n- Full `go test ./...` exit 0; sessquery 86.7%, sessrepo 87.2%; build/vet/gofmt/diff-check clean.\n- Full 59-plant battery re-run on final bytes: all KILLED (4 new profile plants incl. token-preserving from-for-to), harmless control SURVIVED applied, controls exit 0.\n- Notable interaction, recorded honestly: the new closure backstop also refuses the all-zero head, so `N-checkpoint-heads` briefly survived; `TestRev7CheckpointHeadAuthority` now pins the `observation_unavailable` class, restoring the kill as wrong-class instead of silent admission and locking heads-before-profile order.\n\n**Attached:** `TASK-260830-21gygk_results-rev8.md`, `TASK-260830-21gygk_conformance-matrix-rev8.md`, `TASK-260830-21gygk_producer-evidence-rev8.tar.gz`. AC 8/8 established (CLI stays a stated bound). Candidate left uncommitted; branch/HEAD untouched; worktree board copy untouched.","reason":null}}
